{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed single&amp;nbsp;storey rear extension by reason of its siting, excessive rearward depth, bulk and scale would harm the neighbouring amenity of No.111 Torbay Road&amp;nbsp;by way of harmful visual intrusion, outlook&amp;nbsp;and overbearing impacts;&amp;nbsp;and due to the side facing window would lead to actual or the perception of overlooking to No.107, to the&amp;nbsp;detriment of the residential amenities of the occupiers of those neighbouring dwellings. This would be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023) policy D3.D(7) of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 of the Harrow&amp;nbsp;Core Strategy (2012) and&amp;nbsp;Policy DM1 of the Harrow&amp;nbsp;Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:105%&quot;&gt;The two storey&amp;nbsp;side&amp;nbsp;extension, by reason of its inappropriate and incongruous roof form and its relation to the host dwelling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;would result in a discordant&amp;nbsp;and out of keeping addition, which would appear unduly at odds with the established pattern of built form within the area and&amp;nbsp;would be detrimental to the character and appearance of the original dwelling, contrary to the high quality design aspirations set out in&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:105%&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;The National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
